<sheets><sheet><plain><text x="20" y="412" size="3.4" layer="97" ratio="8">POTS Audio Bridge - sound card microphone and headset across a telephone line</text>
<text x="20" y="400" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">Line -&gt; F1 50mA -&gt; R1/R2 100R -&gt; K1 hook relay -&gt; T1 wet 600:600 -&gt; centre-tapped hybrid -&gt; 40 dB pad -&gt; MIC IN</text>
<text x="20" y="392" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">Sound card out -&gt; 15 dB pad -&gt; hybrid TX.  Agent headset hangs off the same hybrid.</text>
<text x="20" y="380" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">DC loop when off-hook: R1 100 + R2 100 + K1 contact + T1 primary 40-150 = 240-350 R, under the 400 R limit.</text>
<text x="20" y="370" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">The hybrid is a Wheatstone bridge of four 620 R arms, one being the line via C, nulled by RV2 470 R.</text>
<text x="20" y="358" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">SAFETY: T1 MUST be the wet type (20-50 mA DC without saturation). A dry voice transformer will saturate.</text>
<text x="20" y="348" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">REGULATORY: this is not an approved interface. Use a certified DAA, or stay on the private side of a PBX.</text>
<text x="20" y="336" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">POTS reference levels: -9 dBm (275 mV into 600 R), 300-3400 Hz, 48 V DC, ring above 150 V peak.</text>
<frame x1="0" y1="0" x2="520" y2="420" columns="8" rows="6" layer="91" border-left="yes" border-top="yes" border-right="yes" border-bottom="yes"/>
<text x="330" y="8" size="2.2" layer="97">POTS Audio Bridge rev A · sheet 1/1 · generated from tools/xport-v92-audiobridge-model.mjs · docs/xport-nucleo-v92-audio-bridge.md</text></plain>
